  "worked_solution": "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta $ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}\u20612\\theta =2{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}\u20612\\theta +1).\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta =2x,$ we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}\u20612x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}\u20614x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4{cos}^{2}\u20612x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}\u20614x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int (\\operatorname{cos}\u20614x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}\u20614x+x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}\u20614x+2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
